# The Bayesian-optimisation stack, locked apart from the rest.
#
# This is the one part of the app that a supported machine can legitimately
# fail to install, so it is not allowed to take the core install down with
# it. See requirements-core.in for why (no macOS x86_64 torch wheel since
# 2.2.2; the arm64 wheel is tagged macosx_14_0, i.e. Sonoma or newer).
#
# Compiled against requirements-core.txt as a constraint, so the shared
# packages (numpy, scipy, ...) resolve to the SAME versions the core lock
# already pinned rather than a second, conflicting set.

botorch==0.18.1
gpytorch==1.15.2
torch==2.12.1
